            "description": "Watch Istanbul Basaksehir vs Inter Turku highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 22, 2026. The stage was set for a high-stakes European encounter as both teams emerged from the tunnel under the floodlights. With a place in the next round on the line, the tactical battle promised to be as intense as the atmosphere in the stands, with neither side willing to give an inch early on. An Early Breakthrough On July 22, 2026 , Istanbul Basaksehir hosted Finnish side Inter Turku in a compelling UEFA Europa Conference League fixture. The home side looked to dominate possession early, but they were stunned in the 16th minute. A clinical counter-attack saw Jasse Tuominen provide a perfectly weighted assist for Clinton Jephta , who clinicaly found the back of the net to give the visitors a shock lead. Basaksehir pushed for a response before the interval, but the Finnish defense held firm until the halftime whistle blew at 45+2'. Bayram Rescues the Hosts The second half began with renewed energy from the home side, though Ousseynou Ba picked up an early yellow card in the 46th minute as frustrations simmered. The pressure finally told in the 54th minute when Yusuf Sari delivered a superb ball into the box, allowing Emin Bayram to power home the equalizer. The goal sparked a wave of tactical changes, with Istanbul Basaksehir introducing Abbosbek Fayzullayev , Davie Selke , and Nuno Da Costa in search of a winner. As the match entered its final stages, the physical nature of the contest intensified. Inter Turku players Jasse Tuominen and Janne-Pekka Laine both saw yellow cards as they fought to protect the draw. Despite late substitutions from both managers, including the introduction of Berat Ozdemir and Iiro Jaervinen , neither side could find a decisive late goal. The referee blew the final whistle at 90+4', confirming a hard-fought 1-1 draw that leaves everything to play for in the return leg."
